WEBVTT

00:01.370 --> 00:03.870
Major! Are you all right?

00:06.740 --> 00:09.730
Who the hell was that guy?

00:11.260 --> 00:13.790
Well done, Colonel Mikel.

00:13.790 --> 00:16.400
It is thanks to the excellent 
training the party gave me.

00:17.330 --> 00:19.570
Why are we letting the enemy escape?

00:19.570 --> 00:23.880
We need to shoot them, and everyone else 
commanded by the Devil of the Rhine!

00:24.170 --> 00:27.320
The party ordered us to surround them.

00:27.320 --> 00:29.550
You're ignoring the opportunity 
that's right in front of you?

00:30.520 --> 00:32.380
Orders are orders.

00:32.380 --> 00:35.220
Are you saying our party is wrong?

00:35.220 --> 00:37.430
Are you saying you can win 
by just following orders?

00:37.430 --> 00:39.400
Lieutenant Sue, that's enough.

00:39.400 --> 00:41.520
He's a commander in an allied army.

00:41.520 --> 00:42.900
Show respect.

00:45.120 --> 00:46.390
Understood.

00:49.740 --> 00:51.850
The Devil of the Rhine...

02:26.580 --> 02:32.080
This story is a work of fiction. People, organizations, locations, laws, names, etc. have no relation to any real-life counterparts.

02:26.740 --> 02:30.330
How could you let someone from that 
volunteer army shoot you down?

02:30.700 --> 02:34.220
It was the Federation. 
A Federation mage...

02:34.220 --> 02:35.270
What?

02:35.270 --> 02:39.730
The Federation purged them as a symbol 
of the old order a long time ago...

02:39.730 --> 02:43.600
I'm... sure of it.

02:44.580 --> 02:46.550
<i>The Federation has mages?</i>

02:47.080 --> 02:49.360
<i>They brought them back from the camps?</i>

02:49.360 --> 02:53.360
<i>The damn Commies are 
that obsessed with us?</i>

02:53.360 --> 02:55.360
<b>Episode Six
Decoy</b>

02:53.980 --> 02:58.020
Men, why are we not 
sending a relief force?

02:55.360 --> 02:58.030
<b>Unified Year 1927, Morning of June 18th</b>

02:59.570 --> 03:02.310
We're going to save 
our surrounded allies.

03:02.310 --> 03:04.540
This should be a very simple matter.

03:04.840 --> 03:09.110
If we can destroy the enemy field army 
that's surrounded the Rerugen Combat Team,

03:09.110 --> 03:12.790
it will help A Group, our main unit.

03:13.140 --> 03:15.260
It's a heroic first step

03:15.830 --> 03:20.310
towards the completion 
of Project Andromeda...

03:20.760 --> 03:25.880
General, the order given to 
B Group is to defend the line.

03:25.880 --> 03:28.340
Think about the state of 
the Empire right now!

03:28.340 --> 03:31.650
A single failure could doom us!

03:31.650 --> 03:35.780
Then we just won't fail.

03:37.230 --> 03:40.770
Resolve. That's what a commander needs!

03:40.770 --> 03:46.540
Use your heart not to hesitate, 
but to make decisions!

03:52.310 --> 03:55.040
<i>Any more discussion is 
just a waste of time.</i>

03:55.750 --> 03:59.550
I understand your concerns.

03:59.550 --> 04:00.820
And so...

04:01.210 --> 04:04.650
You may follow your own hearts.

04:11.400 --> 04:12.670
Oh, you.

04:12.670 --> 04:16.400
Would you please call
Lieutenant Grantz for me?

04:17.820 --> 04:22.480
Very well. I make this request using the 
authority granted to me by Strategic HQ.

04:22.480 --> 04:24.040
I'm counting on you.

04:31.320 --> 04:33.700
Lieutenant Grantz has arrived!

04:34.180 --> 04:36.710
Lieutenant, do you enjoy going for walks?

04:37.630 --> 04:40.270
I've already spoken to 
Division Commander Krum,

04:40.270 --> 04:42.100
who is in charge of our 
strategic reserves.

04:42.100 --> 04:44.440
The other division commanders 
will be joining us as well.

04:44.440 --> 04:47.150
I'm afraid I don't understand...

04:47.800 --> 04:50.440
Soldim 528.

04:50.440 --> 04:54.430
You're aware that the Rerugen Combat 
Team has been surrounded, yes?

04:56.430 --> 04:57.960
Leave it to me!

04:57.960 --> 05:01.450
I'll meet up with Division Commander 
Krum and go rescue them!

05:03.850 --> 05:05.790
Oh, wait.

05:07.670 --> 05:11.830
General, you don't need to see us off...

05:18.790 --> 05:22.040
Please get back, General!

05:22.040 --> 05:23.580
Impossible.

05:23.580 --> 05:28.790
Since the Imperial Army's founding, 
officers have always stood at the front!

05:29.250 --> 05:32.260
Now men, let's leap into the mud!

05:32.550 --> 05:35.920
Let's begin a war together!

05:42.020 --> 05:44.530
<b>Soldim 528</b>

05:44.800 --> 05:47.030
Stay sharp! Watch for ambushes!

05:50.700 --> 05:51.820
Don't shoot yet.

05:52.250 --> 05:54.580
Use a sniping spell to make sure 
you take them down.

05:55.740 --> 05:57.000
Good news.

05:57.000 --> 05:58.600
The rescue army is on the move.

05:59.020 --> 06:00.570
Finally?

06:00.570 --> 06:04.340
And Lieutenant General Zettour 
is heading here as well.

06:04.340 --> 06:06.540
What? He's coming himself?

06:06.550 --> 06:10.800
"From Zettour to Rerugen Combat Team
 Take action immediately"

06:07.770 --> 06:10.800
<i>"Take action immediately."</i>

06:10.800 --> 06:16.630
<i>Does he mean to take strategic action... 
to make the best choice for what to do?</i>

06:17.560 --> 06:20.420
<i>What is General Zettour thinking?</i>

06:23.820 --> 06:25.870
Enemy tank at two o'clock!

06:25.870 --> 06:26.860
Prepare for combat!

06:26.860 --> 06:28.930
<i>Get back, General! Please!</i>

06:28.930 --> 06:33.480
Don't worry. We have a mage as an escort.

06:33.480 --> 06:36.000
Sir, I can't just...

06:41.330 --> 06:42.910
Well done, Lieutenant!

06:42.910 --> 06:44.910
I'm honored, but please fall back!

06:44.910 --> 06:46.880
I'm well aware that we're in 
the presence of the enemy.

06:46.880 --> 06:49.620
I expect you all to deal with them.

06:50.050 --> 06:53.050
<b>Same Night, Federation Soldim Encirclement Command HQ</b>

06:51.280 --> 06:53.060
An enemy relief force?

06:53.060 --> 06:54.900
Yes, Lieutenant Colonel.

06:55.290 --> 06:59.140
Our allies' patrols have 
sighted new enemy forces.

06:59.670 --> 07:04.280
What we believe to be an enemy relief
force has crossed a warning line of ours.

07:04.280 --> 07:06.500
Our forces are in combat now.

07:06.500 --> 07:11.760
And we're sure the enemy 
commander is Hans von Zettour?

07:11.760 --> 07:14.160
According to intercepted 
enemy communications,

07:14.160 --> 07:17.110
we believe it's quite likely.

07:17.490 --> 07:19.300
If it's really him...

07:20.030 --> 07:22.660
Kill him. At all costs.

07:23.120 --> 07:25.340
He's too valuable a target to lose.

07:25.340 --> 07:28.130
We'll go take him out on 
our own if we have to.

07:29.020 --> 07:30.820
Lieutenant Colonel Drake,

07:30.820 --> 07:32.940
I'm afraid I'll have to 
ask you to reconsider.

07:33.550 --> 07:34.550
The goal of this operation is...

07:34.550 --> 07:37.310
Our unit has the authority 
to make its own decisions.

07:38.830 --> 07:42.970
We should go with you, then.

07:42.970 --> 07:44.570
Comrade Colonel!

07:44.570 --> 07:46.440
Comrade Political Officer,

07:46.650 --> 07:50.700
we are fighting against the Empire, 
the enemy of the whole world,

07:50.700 --> 07:53.780
alongside our allies 
on behalf of the party.

07:53.780 --> 07:57.400
And we are expected to press on,
 come what may.

07:57.620 --> 07:59.780
Under these conditions,

07:59.780 --> 08:03.420
we cannot let the unit that our party
 has instructed us to work with

08:03.420 --> 08:05.270
take a risk like this alone.

08:06.680 --> 08:08.620
Very well.

08:08.620 --> 08:10.080
You are correct.

08:10.500 --> 08:12.810
I shall sign the order as well.

08:12.810 --> 08:16.230
So we'll be going together, then?

08:18.480 --> 08:20.360
<i>This is ridiculous.</i>

08:20.800 --> 08:24.470
<i>They need a fancy story just to 
discuss their own operations?</i>

08:26.900 --> 08:29.570
<b>Dawn of the Next Day</b>

08:34.420 --> 08:36.650
New enemies! Eleven o'clock!

08:36.650 --> 08:38.210
New guests?

08:38.210 --> 08:40.600
<i>General, we can't break through!</i>

08:41.240 --> 08:43.670
If the enemy's left their hole 
to come after us,

08:43.670 --> 08:45.720
then I'll be the decoy.

08:46.050 --> 08:46.950
General!

08:46.950 --> 08:49.340
Stop the car.

08:54.260 --> 08:56.100
A pincer attack?

08:56.100 --> 08:57.100
Yes.

08:57.360 --> 08:59.390
This is the current situation.

08:59.760 --> 09:05.200
The enemy was kind enough to meet us
before we arrived at our destination.

09:05.200 --> 09:08.790
The Rerugen Combat Team will be here too.

09:08.790 --> 09:10.740
We'll hit the enemy from both sides.

09:12.390 --> 09:13.750
I see.

09:14.190 --> 09:17.290
So you've worked this out with 
Lt. Colonel Degurechaff in advance.

09:17.290 --> 09:21.610
If that's the case, I would've 
liked to know ahead of time.

09:22.060 --> 09:24.970
No, I came up with the idea just now.

09:26.590 --> 09:28.960
I know Lieutenant
Colonel Degurechaff well.

09:28.960 --> 09:31.390
This sort of thing is well 
within her capabilities.

09:31.390 --> 09:33.470
She's preparing right now, I'm sure.

09:34.730 --> 09:37.540
Sir, even the Lieutenant Colonel...

09:37.540 --> 09:38.540
Lieutenant!

09:38.900 --> 09:43.130
I'm told you all call Lieutenant 
Colonel Degurechaff a monster.

09:43.550 --> 09:45.880
But if you ask me...

09:47.490 --> 09:51.670
That's what a strategy officer should be.

09:54.660 --> 09:55.820
Lieutenant Colonel!

09:55.820 --> 09:57.650
New traffic on Federation comms!

09:57.920 --> 09:59.370
Translate for me!

10:00.850 --> 10:03.230
They've intercepted the relief force!

10:03.230 --> 10:04.730
What's our allies' situation!

10:05.430 --> 10:06.610
The battle is chaotic.

10:07.920 --> 10:10.610
No, they're talking about a major target?

10:10.610 --> 10:11.830
Command functionality?

10:13.250 --> 10:16.470
The enemy's hitting hard because our 
allied command has exposed themselves.

10:16.470 --> 10:17.370
Wait.

10:18.410 --> 10:20.380
<i>Command has exposed themselves?</i>

10:20.890 --> 10:23.110
<i>Would he make a mistake like that?</i>

10:31.090 --> 10:32.740
L-Lieutenant Colonel?

10:33.410 --> 10:37.010
The Lieutenant General isn't such an 
idiot that he can't play hide and seek!

10:37.650 --> 10:39.650
You still don't get it?

10:40.070 --> 10:43.710
Now it's his turn to be the decoy!

10:44.150 --> 10:46.510
B-But why?

10:46.510 --> 10:49.540
There's only one reason you'd focus the 
enemy's attention on a single direction...

10:50.380 --> 10:53.370
So that your buddy can kick 
them hard in the ass!

10:55.350 --> 10:57.390
You don't mean we're going 
out there ourselves...

10:57.390 --> 10:58.630
That's right!

10:58.630 --> 11:01.200
Everyone but the mages 
will remain on defense.

11:01.200 --> 11:03.390
Have Major Weiss take command.

11:04.420 --> 11:07.320
I'm sure he's recovered enough 
to flap his damn lips.

11:07.720 --> 11:08.710
Understood!

11:08.710 --> 11:11.940
The 203rd will head out, keeping our 
magical signature to a minimum!

11:12.390 --> 11:14.600
We'll sneak through the 
enemy's encirclement,

11:14.600 --> 11:17.110
head towards the relief force...

11:20.000 --> 11:23.090
And shove our guns 
right up the enemy's ass!

11:36.250 --> 11:38.010
Begin the attack!

11:44.140 --> 11:47.430
<b>Same Time, Soldim 528</b>

11:44.890 --> 11:46.350
What's the enemy doing?

11:46.350 --> 11:47.440
No change.

11:47.440 --> 11:51.180
<i>They're probably so scared of our 
encirclement they're in hiding.</i>

11:51.440 --> 11:54.070
<i>That's not who the Devil of the Rhine is.</i>

11:56.250 --> 11:57.600
Understood.

11:57.600 --> 12:00.840
We'll continue the encirclement while 
attempting to target General Zettour.

12:01.610 --> 12:03.270
The situation's changed!

12:03.270 --> 12:05.230
The enemy's mages have left their base!

12:05.910 --> 12:09.320
We'll take down the enemy base before 
we take down their reinforcements!

12:09.320 --> 12:11.850
If we turn around after that and 
destroy their reinforcements,

12:11.850 --> 12:12.870
we'll have a total victory!

12:13.380 --> 12:16.430
Lieutenant Colonel,
we cannot alter our orders.

12:16.430 --> 12:19.790
The battlefield has changed, 
and we're adapting to it!

12:19.790 --> 12:20.630
What's wrong with that?

12:20.630 --> 12:23.960
We've already made the preparations 
to take out General Zettour!

12:23.960 --> 12:25.930
We can't just change everything!

12:25.930 --> 12:28.000
The Devil of the Rhine has disappeared!

12:28.000 --> 12:29.190
We can hit while she's gone!

12:33.680 --> 12:37.200
She's... not here?

12:41.370 --> 12:44.190
Damn it! That girl just 
keeps running off!

12:48.530 --> 12:51.290
<b>Sky Above Soldim 528</b>

12:54.120 --> 12:55.950
Magical signature at three o'clock!

12:58.790 --> 13:00.820
We can't just let her go, can we?

13:00.820 --> 13:02.710
Fine! We'll follow her!

13:03.880 --> 13:05.050
HQ!

13:05.050 --> 13:08.810
We will pursue the enemy mages 
that have left the base!

13:10.620 --> 13:14.620
Yes. The Allied Kingdom's unit 
is refusing to work with us...

13:15.230 --> 13:18.390
They just ran off to pursue 
the Devil of the Rhine.

13:21.340 --> 13:23.110
Comrade Political Officer?

13:25.030 --> 13:27.450
The party has given us a new priority.

13:27.450 --> 13:29.820
We are to support the Allied Kingdom,

13:30.080 --> 13:32.940
and if the Devil of the Rhine 
is present,

13:33.350 --> 13:35.740
we are to shoot her down 
and secure her at all costs.

13:39.040 --> 13:41.080
Just a little longer...

13:41.080 --> 13:45.320
We'll be seeing each other soon, 
my little fairy...

13:46.700 --> 13:49.260
Hurry! The enemy will find us!

13:56.190 --> 13:56.890
Got her!

14:09.530 --> 14:10.570
This is 05!

14:11.160 --> 14:12.900
They took the bait!

14:13.750 --> 14:15.240
They fell for the decoy, huh?

14:15.990 --> 14:18.540
That'll make things easier on 
the ones who stayed behind!

14:22.020 --> 14:24.260
No way! No way! No way! Not a chance!

14:24.260 --> 14:26.170
05, disengaging!

14:37.570 --> 14:38.750
<i>She broke past us!</i>

14:38.750 --> 14:40.250
<i>She doesn't play fair!</i>

14:40.250 --> 14:41.350
A decoy?

14:41.350 --> 14:43.060
Damn it. That was smart.

14:44.390 --> 14:47.030
<i>Soldim, or the relief force...</i>

14:47.430 --> 14:48.950
<i>Where is she?</i>

14:49.280 --> 14:51.740
<b>Sky Near the Relief Force</b>

14:50.640 --> 14:51.740
There they are!

14:51.740 --> 14:52.860
Our allies!

14:52.860 --> 14:54.590
Prepare for surface support!

14:54.590 --> 14:56.000
We'll hit them from behind!

15:14.580 --> 15:17.020
That's him, Lieutenant Colonel!

15:17.020 --> 15:19.580
The one who took down Major Weiss!

15:19.580 --> 15:21.460
That Federation mage?

15:21.460 --> 15:23.960
Looks like they knew what we were after.

15:28.580 --> 15:30.030
Unlock the seals on our magic!

15:30.030 --> 15:35.290
Show these heroes from the last era how 
we do long-range combat these days!

15:40.010 --> 15:40.540
What?

15:53.590 --> 15:55.550
How do they work together so well?

15:55.550 --> 15:58.100
The bonds they formed in the camps?!

15:58.950 --> 16:00.060
It's no good!

16:00.320 --> 16:01.810
We can't break their shields!

16:03.260 --> 16:06.730
<i>Federation computation jewel 
technology is that good?</i>

16:12.230 --> 16:14.840
<i>If nothing else, they have strong armor...</i>

16:17.050 --> 16:18.590
We'll try something else!

16:18.900 --> 16:20.360
I'll start with air bombs!

16:20.360 --> 16:22.620
I'm going to burn out their lungs!

16:23.790 --> 16:25.910
O Lord, by your holy name...

16:26.280 --> 16:31.420
Drive away your foes and 
bring peace unto the land!

16:45.490 --> 16:47.910
Compared to the winds in the camps...

16:48.630 --> 16:50.230
That was nothing.

16:57.540 --> 16:59.680
Get back, General!

16:59.680 --> 17:01.750
This is what it all comes down to!

17:01.750 --> 17:04.060
I have to fight as well!

17:12.230 --> 17:13.280
General!

17:15.310 --> 17:17.070
Hmph...

17:17.430 --> 17:21.710
It's times like these when 
I'm jealous of young ones...

17:22.040 --> 17:23.350
We can't go on!

17:23.350 --> 17:26.480
We've lost a whole regiment!

17:26.480 --> 17:28.780
Stop your whining!

17:28.780 --> 17:33.140
If we fall back here, 
our whole army could collapse!

17:33.640 --> 17:34.900
But...

17:36.910 --> 17:39.670
Raise the flag!

17:39.670 --> 17:43.700
Let them know I'm here!

17:57.790 --> 17:59.500
<i>At this rate...</i>

18:05.540 --> 18:07.570
<i>Lieutenant Grantz! It's me!</i>

18:07.570 --> 18:08.810
Lieutenant Colonel!

18:08.810 --> 18:10.150
You came!

18:10.150 --> 18:11.640
<i>I don't have enough men! Help me!</i>

18:13.820 --> 18:15.780
I'll break their shields 
with melee combat!

18:15.780 --> 18:18.240
When I do, hit them from behind!

18:18.240 --> 18:19.150
<i>Understood!</i>

18:19.150 --> 18:20.790
<i>But the General won't 
have any protection!</i>

18:22.160 --> 18:24.620
<i>I don't care. Do it!</i>

18:25.390 --> 18:26.850
But...

18:26.850 --> 18:29.300
I gave you an order!

18:29.300 --> 18:31.020
I can't leave you exposed!

18:34.270 --> 18:35.430
Sir!

18:37.090 --> 18:38.310
Go!

18:40.950 --> 18:43.190
A high-ranking officer will die.

18:43.190 --> 18:44.860
That's a good thing.

18:44.860 --> 18:48.380
It'll wake up those morons 
back home, a little.

18:48.810 --> 18:54.430
The corpse of a soldier must 
be put to the best use it can.

18:54.770 --> 18:58.630
That's what war is all about.

18:59.780 --> 19:01.900
Lieutenant Colonel Degurechaff...

19:01.900 --> 19:04.800
Let me see you dance.

19:07.560 --> 19:11.220
Let me show you a piece of arte, then.

19:22.880 --> 19:24.430
Melee combat!

19:25.960 --> 19:27.430
After me!

19:34.880 --> 19:35.640
Now!

19:36.730 --> 19:40.640
Fire!

19:57.670 --> 19:59.960
Now fucking die!

20:07.630 --> 20:08.900
It's over.

20:13.500 --> 20:16.610
Damn it! The jewel is at its limit?

20:31.270 --> 20:33.420
<i>Enemy mages are retreating!</i>

20:33.420 --> 20:36.020
Ground support! Prepare to charge!

20:36.020 --> 20:38.090
We're going to save the general!

20:38.090 --> 20:39.300
Follow me!

20:47.810 --> 20:50.300
Wipe them all out! Fire!

20:58.060 --> 20:59.140
Sir?

20:59.620 --> 21:02.420
A wonderful piece of arte, indeed.

21:02.420 --> 21:06.080
Let me invite you for tea 
when this is over.

21:06.080 --> 21:08.290
How sophisticated.

21:08.290 --> 21:11.070
A strange thing to say on a battlefield.

21:11.070 --> 21:13.940
Culture is what separates us 
from the beasts,

21:13.940 --> 21:16.720
and divides daily life 
from the extraordinary.

21:17.070 --> 21:18.790
Don't you agree?

23:10.730 --> 23:12.080
Lieutenant!

23:12.080 --> 23:14.780
You lack love for your fellow soldiers.

23:15.700 --> 23:18.580
Wh-What do you mean?

23:25.220 --> 23:28.120
Sorry. I'm a bit peckish.

23:35.970 --> 23:40.000
<b>Next Time
Purgatory</b>
